TITLE: NetMoniAI: An Agentic AI Framework for Network Security & Monitoring
KEYWORDS: Agentic AI systems; Anomaly detection; Large Language Models; Network Security &Monitoring; Network simulation; Autonomous agents; Network security; Open systems; Agentic AI system; AI systems; Anomaly detection; Decentralised; Language model; Large language model; Network Monitoring; Network simulation; Networks security; Security monitoring; Anomaly detection
ABSTRACT: In this paper, we present NetMoniAI, an agentic AI framework for automated network monitoring and security that integrates decentralized analysis with lightweight centralized coordination. The framework consists of two layers: autonomous micro-agents at each node perform local traffic analysis and anomaly detection. A central controller aggregates insights across nodes to identify coordinated attacks and maintain systemwide situational awareness. We evaluated NetMoniAI on both a local micro-testbed and through NS-3 simulations. The results confirm that the two-tier agentic AI design improves response time and maintains accuracy while avoiding duplicate reporting, thereby reducing redundant alerts. In addition, the framework demonstrates scalability across diverse deployment scenarios. The complete framework is available as open source for adoption and reproducibility. This enables researchers and practitioners to replicate, validate, and extend the framework across various network environments and threat scenarios. Github link: https://github.com/pzambare3/NetMoniAI. © 2025 IEEE.
